{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1456882-crossover-question-how-hard-is-it-to-manage-and-dominate-a-cancer-cell","id":1456882,"title":"Crossover Question how hard is it to manage and dominate a cancer cell.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-15T10:33:33-07:00","id":1456882,"title":"Crossover Question how hard is it to manage and dominate a cancer cell.","content":"Think it would be too challenging for a vampire mage, werewolf or geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T12:41:43-07:00","id":1456977,"title":"","content":"Like, an already cancerous cell that already has monsters in it?<br /> <br /> Kinda depends on the monster in question and their personality, as well as the personalities of the hunter cell in question, and how openly cancerous the cell is within itself.<br /> <br /> It's doable as a board question, but the ask is so broad as to almost be useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T19:44:37-07:00","id":1457622,"title":"","content":"Was thinking just to have a cell under your thumb<br /> <br /> The best way to be certain of their loyalty is the conditioning Devotion. Any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T16:41:56-07:00","id":1457659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1456882-crossover-question-how-hard-is-it-to-manage-and-dominate-a-cancer-cell?p=1457622#post1457622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was thinking just to have a cell under your thumb<br /> <br /> The best way to be certain of their loyalty is the conditioning Devotion. Any other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who you are and what sort of chain of loyalty/devotion you're working to make. Vampries and changelings have a lot more options for bringing them under sway than others, but the best cancer cells are those built on actual devotion, where severing the influence is hella hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T12:07:18-07:00","id":1457726,"title":"","content":"I'd also say it depends on what the domination is meant to do, and if it's part of the vigil. Also if the 'turned' individual was part of the cell before. I would say it was based on:<br /> <br /> - Humanity: How easy is it for the splat to be a good guy. More human ones could easily make it, while one's prone to zerking like wolves or vamps are not.<br /> - Domination: Ability to condition.<br /> - Vigilance: The likelihood the splat's goals and the goals of the splat can be coordinated.<br /> - Turning: How the target was turned, and their first experience. A first change that leaves a cell member dead is different that a newborn mage awakening and incinerating the vampire who had the cell one the ropes.<br /> <br /> - Vampires: The beast can make it difficult, and the need for blood makes it difficult. The temptation of ghouling and mind-control powers makes it a bit easier - but between the moral degeneration, need for blood, and frenzy, a vampire would probably have a hard time initially reestablishing trust. And if they weren't part of the cell before, they have close to zero chance of recruiting.<br /> <br /> - Werewolves: The first change could easily leave another cell member dead. That being said? Werewolves hunt. Taking down predatory spirits or the Pure would already fit the vigil. A werewolf pack might even be able to convince hunters to partner with them, in exchange for certain concessions (such as more regard for collateral). Certain egalitarian packs, especially Iron Masters, might even actively try to court a cell, acknowledging their skill at the hunt for what it is. In short, if you can get past that nasty first change, werewolves have good ability to court.<br /> <br /> - Changelings: Changelings, as per usual, have one big issue: fetches. If the fetch dies in front of their eyes and bursts into gum wrappers, they might be more willing to buy the story of the actual former hunter on their return. Especially if the changeling didn't kill them themselves. Changelings are likely to be sympathetic figures. They're not exactly predatory, at least more than humans - most mortals won't even notice a changeling harvest. And truth be told, the Keepers and their total disregard for humanity is something hunters are likely to hate. They are, however, stopped by paranoia. A changeling barely trusts the average mortal, let alone someone dedicated to killing someone like them. A changeling would have to have been a former hunter themselves to have any will to try to convince their former cell. The other possibility is Avowed. Seeing a keeper drag away a human loved one out of the corner of their eye has probably set more than one person to the vigil, and while fae powers may make their friends see them as a witch, it also gives the changelings an in, as the Avowed would obviously want to rescue their friend and kill the keeper who took them. In short, changelings need an in, a contact. But if they do, they have an easy time.<br /> <br /> Mage - Witches! But seriously, mages... probably have a fairly easy time. Why? They're more or less human. They think a lot like humans do, if a bit more obsessed and hubristic. A fairly humble mage could probably more easily get past the 'us vs them' aspect. Mind magic helps though.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters - Sin-Eaters are probably neutral. Unless they were a former cell member, in which case, how they come about is admirable. They were ready to die in the name of the vigil, and almost did. The bargain saved them, and they got right back up and thought. The average cell isn't going to be as interested in ghost welfare as them, but a good Fury has resources.<br /> <br /> Demons - Demons entering a cell... more or less requires a bargain. A hunter who is sick of all this vigil stuff and desperate to get out may sell the vigil to an enterprising demon who wants potential body guards. In that case, the entry is seemless. Until an angel comes. The Angel of the God Machine could easily turn the cell against the 'possessed one', if the Angel has been instructed by the god machine to play up an Abrahamic Angel - and god forbid the demon accidentally bought into the Long Night or another religious compact or conspiracy. Demons can get in easily, but their relationship is among the most fragile once Angels get involved.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - Hahaha, no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T07:41:55-07:00","id":1458347,"title":"","content":"hmmmn on a slightly different question?<br /> <br /> how difficult would slashers be to bring to heel?<br /> <br /> <br /> Circle of the crone could benefit from having them to throw into some test for a hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> speaking of the circle think that &quot;Curse of Aphrodites favor&quot; Could make a tradable boon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T16:42:51-07:00","id":1459706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1456882-crossover-question-how-hard-is-it-to-manage-and-dominate-a-cancer-cell?p=1458347#post1458347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn on a slightly different question?<br /> <br /> how difficult would slashers be to bring to heel?<br /> <br /> <br /> Circle of the crone could benefit from having them to throw into some test for a hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> speaking of the circle think that &quot;Curse of Aphrodites favor&quot; Could make a tradable boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall, it's possible, but not worth it. Slashers murder, and it'd be a huge pain when the mortal police start poking around the supernaturals in question. The few that might be advantageous are situational.<br /> <br /> It depends. Brutes might be dominatable in a fight by a werewolf. who might be able to cowl them. But it would be a lot of effort to make sure the brute isn't killing on the side, or otherwise attracting attention. It probably wouldn't be worth it. Masks would be like trying to coral a rabid tiger - nearly impossible. At best, a vampire could throw a mask in a cage, then dominate it as a disposable shock trooper. Or, you know, they could just find some martial artist or veteran and ghoul them. There is one exception here - the Predator Kings. The Predator Kings would see how poorly a Brute or Mask fits in society, but how skilled a hunter they are, and might decide they would be a worthwhile addition to the pack. They could be cowled like the wild animal they are by a superior predator.<br /> <br /> A Charmer could be more reasonable to get ahold of. Charmers can mask as normal people fairly effectively, and they're potentially open to quid pro quo. If whatever purpose you have for them is in line with their pet peeve, so much the better. However, while effective communicators, unless they're particularly talented, they're once again generally not worth it. For Psychos, it depends. You could probably work with them if their ideal lines up. The thing is, their special ability could be absolutely devestating as assassins - even to major splats. Hand the Psycho a silver knife, and watch them stab a werewolf in the heart. Recruiting a psycho, however, is very much dependent on lining up your cause to their twisted beliefs. Even better if they have good dread powers.<br /> <br /> Undesirables are simultaniously the easiest to recruit and least useful slasher. They're never in a useful position. That being said, they might flock to other monsters, Nosferatu being obvious choices. That being said, your average ghoul or fae-touched is more useful. Overall, Undesirables are easy to recruit, but tend to be a liability. The same could be said of a Mutant, unless their dread powers are particularly good.<br /> <br /> While intelligent, a Virtuoso would be hard to control. They would suffer no situation where they were the puppet, rather than the one pulling the strings. They would rebel given any opportunity. The Puppeteer would need your ideals to match. That being said, there's the possibility that a Beast could bring them around to their point of view - if it doesn't already match. All the Beast has to do is convince them of their lesson, depending on how twisted it is. With a small portfolio already, a Puppeteer would make for a devestating herald.<br /> <br /> Avengers basically are less heeling, more pointing them in the right direction.Keeping them in your work long-term is more trouble than its worth, but if your enemy is guilty of whatever sin the Avenger hates, then they're a deniable asset. A Legend is... annoying. They're so bound to their legend that the only way to really use them is to give your enemies a free weekend stay by Lake Murderstabkill at the Inn of Life and stuff a chicken head into their pillow for good measure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25382,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","user":"Tzauri","date":". 09-11-2021, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T11:26:09-07:00","id":1459758,"title":"","content":"I was thinking Thinking a Crucible as described in the first edition book though you would need Conditioning To completely overwrite their personalitys.to effecttively control them<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-22-2021, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T19:44:59-07:00","id":1460967,"title":"","content":"<br /> Incidently the Sanctified could also use mind controlled slashers to test peoples faith.<br /> <br /> Any idea how beasts could profit from a slasher pawn? Would it be that good at teaching lessons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T20:16:39-07:00","id":1460973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1456882-crossover-question-how-hard-is-it-to-manage-and-dominate-a-cancer-cell?p=1460967#post1460967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidently the Sanctified could also use mind controlled slashers to test peoples faith.<br /> <br /> Any idea how beasts could profit from a slasher pawn? Would it be that good at teaching lessons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sanctified would need a <i>really short leash</i> on a Slasher, and considering a large portion of their bedevilment relies on the horror of temptation, one has to wonder if any Slasher &quot;pet&quot; would be used for their regular activities and more of heretic hunts.<br /> <br /> Regarding &quot;lesson culture&quot;, a slasher isn't terribly useful, considering that lesson culture is primarily there to make of use their nature rather than the Sanctified's mandate-however much use it might be for a Sanctified, it's really <i>not</i> for a Beast.<br /> <br /> In the same way a Prince might value a dragur as a nuclear option for handling a situation, a slasher is more valuable to a calculating Beast (or vampire, for that matter) because there's marginally still a mind that can be....curved along their interests, but need to be handled like hand grenades, or a very wild and irate tiger. The more average Beast on the street is gonna try and get Slasher's hunger for murder focused in a healthier direction, all the while (for once) wondering if they're helping a monster outside of their depth-after all, it's one thing to hunger for blood, the hunt, mysteries, humanity, emotion, closure, memories, souls, and equanmity in monstrous actions, but to hunger flatly for <i>killing straight out</i> is an order of magnitude outside of their depth, an act more familiar to Heroes and the Insatiable and the more depraved members of the Children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T21:06:23-07:00","id":1460978,"title":"","content":"Conditioning gives you a <i>really </i><i>short</i> leash.<br /> <br /> One problem is a Brute Or Mask how to let the tested triumph in a fashion that doesnt kill the slasher who you'd probaly prefer to be able to reuse or loan out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-23-2021, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}